n  director haywood and his crew have  managed to rebuild the original visions  corpse  and the episode ends with this new  eerily white version reactivating  white vision has a robust history in the  marvel comics  he's basically a resurrected vision  without any of the things that actually  make him vision  sure he looks mostly the same and has  the same powers  however much like his colour his  emotions and innate goodness are  gone essentially he's what director  haywood claims vision is  and what he thinks that synthezoid  should be a weapon  comic book readers first saw vision in  white in the 1989  vision quest storyline of avengers west  coast  in the comic run hank pym is the one who  rebuilds vision  after mockingbird betrays vision and the  avengers by aiding in the abduction of  vision  once vision is captured his body is  dismantled scarlet witch ends up seeing  vision or broken apart and splayed out  before pym rebuilds him the caveat that  crops up during the reassembling process  are twofold  vision's red exterior was too damaged to  be restored so he's now ghostly white  and his mind originally crafted in the  comics by using brainwaves from wonder  man  has been wiped leaving him without the  same mind or memories that he once  possessed  the new vision that boots up isn't the  same one that his fellow heroes know and  love  he's all android no humanity this causes  scarlet witch whose vision's wife at  this point  just like in one division to plummet  into a state of deep  dark sadness at the same time scarlet  witch also comes to find out  shocking revelations about her children  twin sons billy and tommy  who are part of one division as well how  white vision comes to be in one division  is quite different  but the end result is evidently the same  director heywood and his sword team have  been rebuilding vision  as part of project cataract in medical  terms a cataract occurs when proteins in  the lens of one's eye begin to break  down  causing 